    "468014d4-57ca-4bb2-a8c7-1c6e67456552": {
      "id": "468014d4-57ca-4bb2-a8c7-1c6e67456552",
      "message": {
        "author": {
          "name": null,
          "role": "assistant"
        },
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "# Team Focus Summary\n\nBased on today's strategy meeting, the priority is **not replacing our existing Meta ads**. Instead, we're building a **second acquisition channel** that works alongside them.\n\nOur current ads will continue driving qualified med spa owners into our high-ticket sales process.\n\nAt the same time, we're going to launch a **low-ticket, self-liquidating funnel** centered around our Memberships & Packages playbook. This gives us another way to acquire prospects who aren't ready to invest immediately while building trust, authority, and a nurture pipeline that eventually converts into high-ticket clients.\n\nThe funnel will look something like this:\n\n1. Lead capture page\n2. $297 Memberships & Packages Playbook\n3. $47 order bump (How to Train Your Team to Sell Memberships & Packages)\n4. $997 complete implementation bundle\n5. Strategy Call booking\n6. Free bonus playbook for showing up to the call\n7. Email nurture sequence driving implementation and ultimately our DFY offer\n\nThe philosophy is simple:\n\n- Continue selling high-ticket directly.\n- Add a second revenue stream.\n- Build authority.\n- Capture buyers who need more trust before investing.\n- Sell implementation instead of information.\n\nThis complements everything we're already doing with Meta rather than replacing it. \ue200filecite\ue202turn0file0\ue202L1-L108\ue201\n\n---\n\n# Bethany\n\n### Immediate Priorities\n\n- Finalize the Memberships & Packages playbook so it's current and aligned with today's methodology.\n- Decide exactly what is included in:\n  - $297 Hero Offer\n  - $47 Order Bump\n  - $997 Bundle\n- Determine which playbooks belong inside the bundle and which remain exclusive to implementation.\n- Review every existing deliverable to ensure messaging matches the current Luxora methodology.\n- Record two funnel videos once Jacques delivers the scripts.\n- Record Gil's new ad scripts.\n- Continue refining webinar strategy as an additional authority channel.\n- Speak with Lawrence Monday regarding his low-ticket implementation funnel and determine if there are ideas worth adapting.\n- Continue building additional case studies and one-pagers for sales.\n- Continue leading Strategy Calls until a qualified closer is hired.\n- Interview and evaluate the new closer candidate.\n- Continue testing webinar + low-ticket strategy without abandoning high-ticket sales.\n\n### Sales / Operations\n\n- Personally take Discovery/Strategy Calls for now.\n- Send Arlene Fireflies recordings rather than live shadowing.\n- Continue interviewing stronger closers.\n- Continue improving client assets and authority positioning.\n\n---\n\n# Jacques\n\n### Funnel Build\n\nBuild the complete Membership Funnel.\n\nStructure:\n\n- Lead Capture Page\n- Hero Offer ($297)\n- Order Bump ($47)\n- Bundle Upsell ($997)\n- Strategy Call Booking\n- Thank You Page\n- Email Nurture\n\n### Deliverables\n\n- Write two VSL scripts for Bethany.\n- Design the Membership Playbook to look like a premium magazine/book rather than slides.\n- Create the complete funnel structure.\n- Build landing pages.\n- Connect Stripe.\n- Build order bump.\n- Build upsell flow.\n- Build booking page.\n- Build thank-you page.\n- Create nurture automation.\n\n### Marketing\n\nDevelop messaging around:\n\n- Lifetime Value\n- Recurring Revenue\n- Enterprise Value\n- Memberships\n- Packages\n- Retention\n- Patient Lifetime Value\n\nContinue running existing Meta campaigns while testing the new funnel.\n\n### CRM\n\n- Move Discovery Calendar back to Bethany.\n- Add Aanchal as secondary.\n- Remove Arlene from Discovery routing.\n- Keep attribution reporting separating:\n  - Luxora Leads\n  - AC Leads\n- Continue tracking qualified vs. unqualified lead sources.\n\n---\n\n# Aanchal\n\n### Sales Operations\n\n- Continue owning Discovery scheduling.\n- Handle Discovery Calls where appropriate.\n- Coordinate Bethany's Strategy Calls.\n- Keep Bethany's calendar updated.\n- Continue organizing all call notes.\n\n### Sales Documentation\n\n- Continue improving SOPs.\n- Finish onboarding documentation for future closers.\n- Maintain GHL training documentation.\n- Maintain sales tracking spreadsheet.\n- Keep Fireflies organized and distributed.\n\n### Marketing Support\n\n- Continue assisting with:\n  - Case studies\n  - One-pagers\n  - Sales assets\n  - Webinar organization\n  - Funnel documentation\n  - Course organization\n\n### Client Success\n\n- Coordinate client meetings.\n- Keep implementation meetings moving.\n- Help prepare launch materials for Amari and future clients.\n\n---\n\n# Biggest Strategic Decisions From This Meeting\n\n- Continue running existing Meta ads while testing a second acquisition channel.\n- Launch a low-ticket funnel instead of waiting until everything is perfect.\n- Sell implementation, not information.\n- Lead with Memberships & Packages because it's the most universal pain point.\n- Use every purchase to naturally transition buyers into booking a Strategy Call.\n- Build nurture around implementation since most buyers won't actually execute on the information they purchase.\n- Shift Bethany back into closing until a stronger salesperson is in place.\n- Continue positioning The Luxora Collective as the authority that helps med spas turn one-time patients into lifetime clients rather than simply generating more leads. \ue200filecite\ue202turn0file0\ue202L109-Lend\ue201"
          ]
        },
